WEBVTT

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:33.170
Yes?

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.180
Oh! Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.470
You said you had an interest in these old chateaus.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:45.400
Forgive me for the abruptness.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.690
Don't be, I'm happy to help in your case.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.860
Now then, you may go ahead and observe as you wish.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.700
So what do you think?

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.580
A great design, right?

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:07.210
It was built in the mid-16th century and used to belong to aristocrats.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:11.210
Truth be told, I bought this place just a little while ago.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.470
It was literally love at first sight.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.800
This is the reception hall.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.220
They probably held their dance parties here long ago.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.770
This is quite a view.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:32.780
Isn't it?

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.120
Oh... that's right!

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.540
Would you like some wine?

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:47.960
Since we were destined to meet or something, let's have a drink.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:53.960
Oh, since I love wine more than life
itself, I've built up quite a collection.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.800
I have some vintage labels that I know you'll love.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.970
It'll only take a minute.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.450
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.660
Huh, sir?

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.930
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.060
wondering what I should do right now.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:55.530
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:02:55.690 --> 00:03:00.070
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:05.700
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:11.120
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.590
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:21.880
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:26.180
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:31.270
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:37.360
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:42.950
depend on me for your repairs.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.330
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:53.540
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.840
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:03.890
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:15.020
Proud Wine

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.080
Look, he's buying up everything again.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.830
Hah.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.840
As if he even has a palate for wine.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:43.840
He's not going to outbid us this time.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:50.310
Okay, here we have high-quality red wine from Côte d'Or.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:58.690
There is one 1800 vintage and nine 1900 vintage Romanée-Monts Luisant, making ten bottles altogether.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:00.440
We will start at 10,000 euros.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:02.690
15.

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:04.200
20,000!

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.360
25!

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.200
28,000!

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.200
Do we have any other bids?

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.210
35,000!

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.670
That's 35,000 euros.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.210
Do we have any other bids?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.670
Anyone?

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:28.970
45,000!

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.970
We have 45,000.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:34.730
50,000!

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.230
60,000.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.900
6... 63,000!

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:42.150
70,000.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.150
We have 70,000 euros...

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.160
70,000 euros...

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.120
Do we have any other bids?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:58.170
Very well, sold for 70,000 euros.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.170
So how did it go?

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.170
As we feared, Yanagida outbid us.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.430
I see.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:15.310
That guy doesn't have a taste for good wine!

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:18.520
He just wants to beat people over the head with his wallet!

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:21.900
That's <i>our</i>  wine, the Romanée-Monts Luisant!

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.440
Plus it's our 1800 vintage he'll be drinking to boot! That's a sacrilege against wine itself!

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.950
This vexes me to no end as a Frenchman!

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:33.580
It's nothing to be vexed about, Jacques.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:37.710
This is a fight we the French have already won.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:38.830
Huh?

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:45.550
I knew all along that Yanagida would be the highest bidder at today's auction.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:51.970
If... If you knew that, then you shouldn't
have put the 1800 vintage up for auction!

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:56.180
Then Yanagida wouldn't be in possession of it now.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:57.890
Nope.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.100
Quite the opposite.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:06.650
I actually wanted Yanagida to be the highest
bidder for the 1800 Romanée-Monts Luisant.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.740
Wha... What do you mean by that, sir?

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:16.450
The bottle for that "1800 vintage" actually contains the 1905 vintage.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:24.090
I don't think he'll be able to tell the wine is from 1905 anyway.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:28.340
Have you heard, Jacques?

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.640
In Germany, violating the wine laws is an aristocrat's crime.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.220
That means it's just as honorable as engaging in duels.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:40.730
This was a duel between us and Yanagida.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:44.480
And we've just won the bout.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:50.490
Are you sure about doing this?

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.740
I'm sure.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:08:00.960
That unrefined palate of his can't distinguish between an 1800 or a 1905 vintage.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.480
Does it please?

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.360
Yes, I'll have it.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:46.420
I must confess, I can't make out the slight differences in taste between wines.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.000
You and me both.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:54.380
As a négociant, I always feign a knowing
look on my face, then take notes afterwards

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:58.430
whenever I sample the wine from the casks they send from the breweries.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.930
I really can't tell the difference between the wines myself.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:05.520
Really?

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:06.480
Well...

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:14.490
...I do tell the breweries that I'll no longer trade with them if they sell me bad wine even once.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:19.660
You need trust in order to go into the wine trading business.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:23.500
However, there are a lot of people who betray that trust.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:30.040
We Japanese have a difficult time building those trust-based relationships in France.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.510
It's the same thing for us Germans.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:38.510
The French do have their share of overly prideful people.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.720
Albert is among the worst.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.520
The owner of the Romanée-Mont Luisant...

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.440
...Jean Charles Albert?

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.150
Correct.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:56.530
The Romanée-Mont Luisant red wine is a rare gem that France boasts to the world.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:01.910
Still, Albert simply has too much pride in his wine.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:09.790
Have you heard?

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:11.170
Huh?

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.670
This happened five years ago.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:20.680
The Arab royal family bought the 1800 vintage Romanée-Monts Luisant from Albert.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.680
However...

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:27.180
...the bottle did not contain the 1800 vintage.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:32.690
Once the royal family realized that, they came storming back to Albert's firm.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.400
That's a terrible accusation you're making.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.320
Well, I can understand.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:42.740
The very idea that you Arabian gentlemen would know

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:50.420
the luxurious taste of French wine, let alone our firm's Romanée-Monts Luisant is ridiculous in its face!

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:52.920
Are we clear?

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:57.170
To us the French, that is not some liqueur.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:01.090
That is the creation of our pride and heritage.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:07.310
That means you have just insulted the very country of France

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:11.690
based on a silly misunderstanding by your uncultured palates!

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:13.690
Have you no shame?!

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:20.780
Upon saying that, he had them thrown out.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.330
Did that really happen?

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.330
That means, Yanagida-san...

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:31.420
...whether or not my 1800 vintage is authentic.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:35.420
That's right, so you need to be a little wary.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:39.920
I believe that it is the genuine article.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:43.430
But if it's a fake...

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:47.430
Then that would mean trouble for Albert.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:48.430
Eh?

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:08.080
What is...

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.080
...the meaning of this?

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.180
Oh that's right, take a look at the paper.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:33.140
Yanagida is having a display party at a manor.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:39.360
He's going to present the wine bottles he got at the auction the other day.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:47.120
He also invited five French sommeliers to that party.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:54.080
This is the list of the sommeliers he's inviting.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:02.590
I knew it, Louis Bouvet is also being invited.

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:06.840
He's France's number one sommelier.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:12.600
Any other sommelier probably
couldn't tell that the wine is a fake.

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:16.400
But Louis definitely can.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:22.150
He has drunk the real 1800 vintage before.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:27.610
He's a man that never forgets the taste of a wine.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:33.120
Then he's going to know that the 1800 vintage is a fake at Yanagida's party!

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:39.880
If that happens, the reputation of France's best red wine, the Romanée-Monts Luisant, will...

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:44.760
...be completely obliterated.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:00.690
Louis!

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:07.650
Ah, sorry to call you here when you're so busy.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:15.160
Sorry to be blunt, but what's the matter of business?

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:19.670
It seems you were invited to Yanagida's party.

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.210
Will you be attending?

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:23.920
It's what I intend to do.

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.220
Hmm, well...

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:31.390
Aren't people like you supposed to refuse these things?

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:32.350
Huh?

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:38.390
He's someone who uses his wealth to buy up the wine
even though he cannot distinguish between their tastes.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:44.150
It would hurt your prestige if you showed up at his party.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:50.160
It will be a blotch on your brilliant career as a sommelier.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.620
I see.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:54.160
That is something to think about.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:55.910
That's right.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.660
Still though...

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:03.420
...I don't consider it as an invitation from Yanagida.

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:07.170
What do you mean by that?

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:15.850
I consider it an invitation from Romanée-
Monts Luisant's 1800 and 1900 vintage.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:21.190
A sommelier like me never gets such a splendid invitation.

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:26.530
It would be a blasphemy against
wine to refuse such an invitation.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:31.530
Someone who did that cannot call himself a sommelier.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:47.300
<i>I do appreciate your concern, but I fully intend to attend the party.</i>

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:49.720
Excuse me.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:54.180
Your mail.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.800
Thank you.

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:14.570
"FOR A TRUSTING RELATIONSHIP"

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:16.450
"FOR A TRUSTING RELATIONSHIP"

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.410
Marvelous wine.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.420
Now then, if I may have the sommeliers come here.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:23.310
The one to uncork the 1800 vintage will be...

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.520
...Monsieur Albert!

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.440
If you'll please.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.940
Oh... no! I couldn't possibly...

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:33.900
I cannot think of anyone other than you..

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:38.910
...who has made France's best red wine, the Romanée-Monts Luisant, to do the honors.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.450
Don't you think so, everyone?

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:43.370
That's right!

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.750
Magnificent!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.750
So, Monsieur Albert, if you please.

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:16.360
<i>A bottle of wine?</i>

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:17.950
<i>Yes.</i>

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:22.410
<i>The 1800 Romanée-Monts Luisant. That is your target.</i>

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:31.380
<i>Yes, I only want to get rid of a single bottle of wine, but it's a job that only you can do.</i>

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:06.080
Huh? What happened?

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:11.880
Oh my, this is bad.

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.590
What happened?

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:14.210
Indeed.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.090
Wh- What the...?

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:17.300
This isn't good.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:18.260
What just...?

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:19.590
What a waste.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.600
What happened, Monsieur Albert?

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.650
<i>Tomorrow night...</i>

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:37.570
...there will be a party at Chateau Fontainebleau.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:45.620
I'll also be attending. My 1800 vintage that will be presented there is a fake.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:50.210
But I want to keep that fact from being exposed there.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:56.920
If that happens, the good name of Albert family and
the legend of the Romanée-Monts Luisant will be lost.

00:19:57.420 --> 00:20:00.720
Not to mention all my pride.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:06.890
Who made the fake wine?

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.890
Well...

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:14.900
It was me.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:22.900
So your good name, your legend, and your pride follow from you making fake wine?

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:29.450
S... So, will you accept my request?

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.130
I'll accept.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:38.170
You're really going to accept?

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:42.760
I don't know what I'd do if you didn't take the job.

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:52.430
The fake 1800 vintage will be uncorked at the party.

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:55.560
That is when I want you to shoot.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:21:01.740
The one who'll unknowingly uncork the fake 1800 vintage will probably be drunk with honor.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:08.490
Naturally, if the person knew the wine was going to be
shot through, he'd probably be fumbling around with it...

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:14.580
Oh, it'd probably be a different case if that someone knew you'd be the one shooting.

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:23.090
This is the real 1800 Romanée-Monts Luisant.

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:24.630
By all means.

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:32.850
So how do you like the taste of it?

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:36.350
It's bitter.

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:51.280
Pride is an eminent trait, but too much will cause arrogance.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:54.750
That is when it becomes disgusting.

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:04.630
Are you all right, Monsieur Albert?

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:12.140
Wh... What does some oriental know about the taste of true wine?!

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:23.150
<i>Pride is an eminent trait, but too much will cause arrogance.</i>

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:26.240
<i>That is when it becomes disgusting.</i>

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:45.800
I enjoyed the little things.

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:53.010
I loved when you gave me a flower every day

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:59.100
instead of just one big bouquet

00:22:59.810 --> 00:23:03.940
of flowers.

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:11.570
It was like a romance novel.

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:16.160
Surely someday... just kidding.

00:23:16.490 --> 00:23:19.540
I had a dream.

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:25.250
Your face shined eternally.

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:31.840
Because I think of you all the time.

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:37.390
I'm sorry, but on a lonely night like this

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:43.900
I'm remembering you, but

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:48.490
I won't cry like I did that day.

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:51.660
I won't.

00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:12.010
In order to kill a real-estate mogul on a theater outing, Golgo planned a surprise attack.

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:15.010
Perfect alibi and disappearing weapon.

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:19.850
Now, the curtains will rise on this murder drama.

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:23.940
Next time on Golgo 13: The Night of the Murder Play.

00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:27.650
The Night of the Murder Play

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:29.820
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
